} {:db/id "q-330831" :question/id #uuid "84ac39af-5a4f-5a7b-bd9f-24d50174d342" :question/math-academy-id "q-330831" :question/problem "Given that $L{{t}^{n}}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}$ for $s>0$, find the Laplace transform of\n$g(t)={\\int }_{0}^{t}{τ}^{3}\\,\\text{d}τ$\nfor $s>0.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(t)={t}^{3}.$ Thus, for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =L{f(t)} \\\\  & =L{{t}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3!}{{s}^{3+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the integral identity above, we have that for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{g(t)} & =L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}{τ}^{3}\\,\\text{d}τ} \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{s}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330831/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241972f-4023-5638-aa7a-9e4a75167c3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330831"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-330825/selection/689672a08b28fba294c58d7c7551b966529c1867da17fdb3ae1b4ced60fec7d8" :answer/id #uuid "a39393a5-8aec-542d-80f4-8aef6a099765" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330825/selection/2c3caaca8365b7ba977c330c0dd8d9661b322b56d81b86cd9aefa760e9a9d73c" :answer/id #uuid "1179d763-9a04-5b0e-ab1f-1aed32a7f80c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330825/selection/8b766bebdb3c5c630772a983027e3b9e7e594a93ac66deb598448bcde6d1c7da" :answer/id #uuid "dcf0ac34-4b2e-508c-aafc-04ab91865ac9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s}{s-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-330825/selection/1baf136ef87d4e06f889927c7b104006e460580ff14d93c8eac78e1b5e523a19" :answer/id #uuid "7a83e2d2-6ad2-5163-9953-40c98334a6af" :answer/type :answer.ty