c-5d5d-9bd6-937f20d64110" :question/math-academy-id "q-330849" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s-5)},\\,s>5\n$$\n\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s),$ given that\n$L{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\text{ }s>a.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we can write $G(s)$ as \n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s-5)}=\\frac{F(s)}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $F(s)=\\frac{1}{s-5}.$\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\nL{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a}.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{F(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s-5}} \\\\  & ={e}^{5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nUsing the property above in reverse, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{G(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{F(s)}{s}} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{5τ}\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5τ}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{5t}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-330849/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a65eeb21-bcd5-542d-8277-04dab7fa9b53"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-330849"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327935/selection/e568b9a0afd85af98acbc126d85ff976db1bdcb0de83b1f416d7e95be9ef90b3" :answer/id #uuid "b9175d08-909c-5c51-8ea2-6de9bea4e802" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327935/selection/2a6429c9bc16d718a077b71296c17d64632de81c57e78553e445328955dd4e90" :answer/id #uuid "692043f4-7e66-506a-ba5e-49fcbb403441" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327935/selection/a1c50e4bf1d9809c888fd90e38c90c9e992782bca8b15d970f4ade542b8711b9" :answer/id #uuid "0fbefa14-9f99-5313-bb03-ead214d140f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327935/selection/8a03b9c0b3e68059036021baf77bbfcdf70af9afd9fa60ae83c646da9c396538" :answer/id #uuid "69a354d5-45fa-54a4-bb04-9a17b49a739d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327935/selection/63929de75caee22985633977b80e43113b0604ca2191480a03d061f70005c60d" :answer/id #uuid "2bea080b-d507-5198-a78e-e08d7fd92ced" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327935/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "96da93bb-f22c-5fc6-bf98-b209ef94ad3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-327935/selection/a1c50e4bf1d9809c888fd90e38c90c9e992782bca8b15d970f4ade542b8711b9" :answer-field/choices ["q-327935/selection/e568b9a0afd85af98acbc126d85ff976db1bdcb0de83b1f416d7e95be9ef90b3" "q-327935/selection/2a6429c9bc16d718a077b71296c17d64632de81c57e78553e445328955dd4e90" "q-327935/selection/a1c50e4bf1d9809c888fd90e38c90c9e992782bca8b15d970f4ade542b8711b9" "q-327935/selection/8a03b9c0b3e68059036021baf77bbfcdf70af9afd9fa60ae83c646da9c396538" "q-327935/selection/63929de75caee22985633977b80e43113b0604ca2191480a03d061f70005c60d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327935" :question/id #uuid "8f8057e6-82f2-5886-becf-1eb97b378527" :question/math-academy-id "q-327935" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s({s}^{2}+{\\pi }^{2})},\\,s>0\n$$\n\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s),$ given that\n$L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t)}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we can write $G(s)$ as \n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s({s}^{2}+{\\pi }^{2})}=\\frac{F(s)}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $F(s)=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+{\\pi }^{2}}.$\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t)}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{F(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+{\\pi }^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{L}^{-1}{\\frac{\\pi }{{s}^{2}+{\\pi }^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we know that if $L{f(t)}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nUsing the property above in reverse, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{G(s)} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{F(s)}{s}} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{\\pi }^{2}}\\,(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-327935/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a65eeb21-bcd5-542d-8277-04dab7fa9b53"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327935"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331084/field-1/80cb8dde8b59b402c6d735a0a8c52d5bca720d5210f837ebff44a703d3712643" :answer/id #uuid "8f3c7730-e4a2-5af3-8513-9c1338a8bb6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{A}^{′}(τ)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331084/field-1/031fce1448202d7aaf3d8c8d118c193598bdb1dffcc45f4609cb6fd3ca4e0ac0" :answer/id #uuid "04f4c794-b54e-52a1-a7bd-8387dc9f3dc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(τ)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331084/field-1/59d245aee1140364e2a417c7e8fd5509b1bc6fbadb3cd50592a9c1eda2e87c49" :answer/id #uuid "82821487-e7bc-5d5f-bc8f-5c414475b01f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A(τ)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331084/field-1/2e41713b0907c9bc246492b268c8e34c89aa3370243a26767a25f966e8950f45" :answer/id #uuid "1174f08a-d27d-5f1e-bf18-6124fe73cf05" :answ