7453d89d405d023770b3435d60a8ae89935d1" "q-331084/field-6/d3607a5de05a391ce21dea0e932e55f7fb0545372e75deb4fbf8a1e2e510f940" "q-331084/field-6/20979e2357355a97329dc980a8f2c18ff9d97b4d082f375b13ebd49af3cd7d0d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331084" :question/id #uuid "8bfadb68-c634-5617-a1c3-ca1ddae49650" :question/math-academy-id "q-331084" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find $L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ}$ given $L{f(t)}=F(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.Let $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ={{field-1}}\\,{|}_{0}^{t}=A(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ}=L{A(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-2}}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & ⇒ & du={A}^{′}(t)\\text{ }dt \\\\ dv={{field-3}} & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({{field-4}}){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=$ $0$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{{field-5}}\\,\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={{field-6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ & =A(τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =A(t)-A(0) \\\\  & =A(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ} & =L{A(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & \\,⇒\\, & du={A}^{′}(t)\\,dt \\\\ dv={e}^{-st}\\,dt & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A(0)=0$ and $\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ we have $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=0$ and\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot F(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331084/field-1" "q-331084/field-2" "q-331084/field-3" "q-331084/field-4" "q-331084/field-5" "q-331084/field-6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51dfecdb-ad66-5e07-8873-ca8e116b27bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331084"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220181 :answer-field/correct 17592186220184 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331052/field-2/674760f6a77d4f7658d0345705586090b4a06791d5a25a85db72893a8f7297ae" :answer/id #uuid "26013260-50a2-57bc-8e6f-018f5dd03a81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-st}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331052/field-2/3271feb643933511cd7b0e1eb04d9a734d471e9f34975f85c7afcf6213418e66" :answer/id #uuid "e18775e9-dd92-56fe-baf9-cc96f8ca69b0" :answer/type :answer.t